00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.310
It's too sweet! She got me!

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.320
And now that you can taste it,
it's far too late to fix it!

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.360
My beautiful curry...

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.530
Poor, poor Keiichi!

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.200
Yes, poor, poor Keiichi!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.750
You little... Satoko!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.380
Hey, you still managed to pull through,
despite everything.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.670
Words aren't gonna
make me feel better right now.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.090
If you want me to feel better,
get me something to eat.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.810
I'm sure your dinner will taste great
after all that waiting.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.140
All right, I'm gonna head off to work now.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.950
Hey, you.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.350
Door's open!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.940
G-Good evening...

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.030
Whoa, Kei-<i>chan</i>, why are you on the floor?!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.290
Thanks for the food. It was awesome.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:48.600
Last night, when I was super hungry,
Shion came by and gave me a bunch of food.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.430
So here are all the containers.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.180
I already washed them for you!

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:56.230
O-Oh, wow! Shion's so thoughtful.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.150
My, Mion-<i>san</i>, you sure are
in good humor today!

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:03.740
Yeah! She's being so kind and gentle.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.220
Look at them! They're so cute!

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.890
I know this place...

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:38.150
If I said I wanted one...

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:41.020
Would you buy one for me, Kei-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.490
Excuse me! I'd like to buy that doll
with the dress in the window!

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:50.320
Sure!

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.410
Let me get--

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:52.780
Mion?!

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.870
K-Kei-<i>chan</i>?!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.040
And why the hell are <i>you </i>here?!

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.170
C'mon, let's go, Kei-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.380
We're not quite done with our date yet!

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.300
W-Wait...

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.720
My sister is hard at work.
We wouldn't want to interrupt.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.850
Okay.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.400
Kei-<i>chan</i>...

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.110
Why?

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.780
June

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.780
Sunday

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:44.000
There are so many stalls!
I wonder if we'll find anything kyute!

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.970
What's up?

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.630
Oh, nothing.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:54.850
First, we gotta find Rika-<i>chan</i>.
Satoko should be with her.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.180
Right.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.400
You just need to drop me off, that's all.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.150
I don't want to hear any business
about "coming with me," Kasai.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:09.030
Very well. Do be careful of
your surroundings at the festival.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.530
What do I need to be careful for?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.530
Hinamizawa can be quite
dangerous this time of year.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.170
What, is the Shotgun Dragon
scared of Hinamizawa, too?

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.920
The village has a history.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:28.210
Even if they really do demon away people,
I can hardly see why they'd take me.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:37.180
By the way, Shion-<i>san</i>, how do you
intend to return home tonight?

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.850
No idea.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:43.440
Maybe I'll ask my sister if
I can stay over at the mansion tonight.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.610
You're going to ask to stay over
at the mansion tonight of all nights?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.490
I'm going to nap until we get there.
Wake me up when we do.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.700
There's a blanket in the back.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.160
But we'll be there very soon.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.660
Shush! It's naptime!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.010
Huh? Where's Kei-<i>chan</i>?

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.140
He was with us until just now.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:21.180
Knowing Keiichi-<i>san</i>, he probably
got dragged off somewhere by Shion-<i>san</i>!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.140
Oh, o-okay!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.860
He's gonna miss Rika-<i>chan</i>'s dance, though.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:30.530
Don't worry! I'm sure he's
somewhere where he can watch!

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:31.860
Yes, I'm sure.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.200
The two of them are likely
having a <i>wonderful </i>time.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.200
Got it open.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.370
Thank you!

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.160
It's finally time.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.380
Well? You're our partners in crime, now.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.880
Would you like to come
take a look with us?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.260
Wh-What? We don't want to be
partners in crime with you or--

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.590
It sounds interesting! Let's go look.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:54.900
Hurry!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.950
If what you said about
the Final Operation is true,

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.160
then the Mountain Dogs
aren't going to let us get away!

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.540
If we can get to the clinic,
we can use my car--

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.910
No way, they've probably got
a tracker on it!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.460
Same with my bike!

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.470
Excuse me, sir, but could we
borrow you for a moment?

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:21.180
Ah, jeez. It happened again this year?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.020
Right, then. I'll want to ask you
for the full story later...

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:30.400
My, if it isn't Mayor Kimiyoshi!

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:33.320
What's going on, Ooishi-<i>san</i>?

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.650
Not another demoning away, I hope.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:40.860
Depending on what happened, yes, perhaps.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.410
What happened, then?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:46.370
About 30 minutes ago, Tomitake-<i>san</i>
and Takano-<i>san </i>came to this parking lot

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.250
and stole one of the trucks parked here.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.750
What? They stole a truck?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:57.420
Yes, according to people
who witnessed the crime...

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.430
Hey, that's the nurse
from Dr. Irie's clinic.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:04.600
Jiro-<i>san</i>!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:05.380
Is the key in there?!

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.470
It sure is!

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:09.390
I'll drive! You get in on the other side!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.020
Hey, that's my truck!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:21.160
Tomitake's that young guy from Tokyo,
right? Why'd he want to steal a car?

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:25.830
Witnesses say they were in a great hurry.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.040
That, or terrified of something.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:32.960
They didn't even bother to load
their belongings into the truck.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.420
They must have been in quite the rush.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.750
Sounds like it.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:37.880
What do you think?

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:42.890
To me, it seems like something scared them
into running out of the village.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.720
I haven't the slightest.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.270
What do you think they'd be
running from, anyway?

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.060
Oh, I don't know...

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.230
...Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.570
What?! Th-That's ridiculous!

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:00.400
I'm only kidding.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.410
An officer is going around
interviewing witnesses.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.490
I've heard some interesting stories
about what happened tonight.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:15.460
Like the two people our criminals
were spotted with earlier.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:19.000
I was just about to go meet with them.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:26.180
I hope they know something
about what's going on.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.900
Kasai? I told you I would manage
getting home on my own.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.030
I'll leave once I give you this.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.780
This is for you, Shion-<i>san</i>.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.740
Huh?

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.780
To protect yourself.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.540
Oh, do be careful with it.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.290
It's an <i>off-market </i>model.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.630
I can see that.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:03.260
Just pulling it out
or buzzing it at someone

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:07.760
should scare them out of trying
any funny business with you.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.600
You're this worried about me?

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.890
Thanks, Kasai.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.270
Of course.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:18.730
Though I don't think anyone
could get to me through our security.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.820
Take it just in case. Good night.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:52.390
Hello there, Shion Sonozaki-<i>san</i>.

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:54.930
Could I have a few minutes of your time?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:59.350
Working this late at night, Uncle Ooishi?

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:05.110
Well, only 'cause it seems I need
to talk with you and Maebara-<i>san</i>!

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:10.200
You were the last people to talk
to Tomitake-<i>san </i>and Takano-<i>san</i>.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.200
What? What do you mean?

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.500
Maebara residence.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.880
Kei-<i>chan</i>! It's me, Shion.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.720
Hey. Why're you calling me so late?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:31.010
I was worried about my sister.
Did she believe your story?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.140
I was worried when she realized
I didn't watch Rika-<i>chan</i>'s dance,

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.850
but she bought it.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.190
That's my sweet Kei-<i>chan</i>.

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:40.940
Oh, shut it, Shion!

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:46.030
So there's... something else
I wanted to ask.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:49.700
Tonight, at the Watanagashi festival,

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.830
all four of us went into
that storehouse, right?

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.630
What's that supposed to mean?

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:08.010
It means that maybe, they were being
targeted by Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:11.550
If they were, then we know the reason.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.560
Why the hell are <i>you </i>going on and on
about how bad it was

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.720
to sneak into the sacred storehouse
on the night of Watanagashi?!

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.600
I'm sorry. I didn't think
this would happen...

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.860
I had nothing to do with all of this!

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:26.610
So now what?! What're you gonna do, huh?!

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.940
Shion.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.990
How're you gonna make this right, huh?!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.370
Hey! Say somethi--

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.630
M-M-Mion...

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.380
Care to explain what's going on?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.800
I-It's not what you think, Mion!
Just let me explain!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:58.520
You dragged Kei-<i>chan </i>into this?
And now he's being targeted by the curse?

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:04.400
Kei-<i>chan</i>... kind, loving Kei-<i>chan</i>...

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.360
...is going to die because of you?

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:17.330
I'm not done talking, Shion.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:23.370
S-Stay back!

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.670
Don't come any closer!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:38.100
It's your fault Oyashiro-<i>sama</i>'s curse
is targeting Kei-<i>chan</i>.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:41.980
If something happens to Kei-<i>chan</i>,
it'll all be your fault.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.850
<i>Your fault</i>, Shion.

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.610
Give him back. Give Kei-<i>chan </i>back to me.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:50.530
I told you to stay back!

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:57.070
Who's after Kei-<i>chan</i>?
You must know, right?

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.160
Has Kasai-<i>san </i>told you anything?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:00.290
I don't know.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.790
Who in the village gave the order?

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:03.960
I don't know!

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.830
It's our old Gran, isn't it?

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:11.090
Out of the Three Houses, Oryo is always
the one pulling the strings.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:14.800
I don't know! I don't! Why would I know?!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.850
Please, don't...

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.930
Mion!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.450
Where are you going?
We're not finished yet.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:55.050
P-Please... stop...

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:58.760
I really don't want to do this.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.360
But I <i>have </i>to do this.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:14.690
Someone has to put an end
to this old, tired tradition.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:21.830
As the next head of the Sonozaki Family,

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:23.700
it's my duty to end it.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.160
To expel the evil from our village.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:29.710
And...

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.720
...to protect Kei-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:44.010
So please, Shion, help me.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:47.390
Just tell me everything you know.

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:56.990
Shion?

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.620
Did I... kill...

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.880
Did I kill Shion...?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.010
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, Shion!

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:46.160
Don't worry, Shion.
I'll see this through to the end.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:51.870
I'll do it for Kei-<i>chan</i>.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.510
There's something
I want to ask you, Grandma.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:08.680
You said before that the Sonozakis
had nothing to do with the curse...

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:14.020
...but you'll tell me the truth, right?

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Wataakashi-hen:
Cotton-Revealing Chapter, Part 3

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:49.870
Next time: "<i>Wataakashi-hen</i>:
Cotton-Revealing Chapter, Part 3."
